<p>Demerara Rum is made by fermenting molasses, which results in sweeter, rounder, and usually darker rum.</p>
<p>All Demerara Rum is distilled in Guyana by <a href="https://www.newworlder.com/guide-to-guyana-demerara-rum/" rel="noopener">the last remaining Guyanese distiller, Demerara Distillers Limited</a> – aka DDL.</p>
<p>The rum is produced on the banks of the Demerara River using the sugarcane grown nearby.</p>
